  "body": "## Scope and dependency\n\nDepends on draft PR #345 at dbe975d3143446c5e7cd9b132b6f994067065e7b. This is a focused correction to the existing event transition function, not a second event or authorization system.\n\nAbsent and unreadable POST targets now return the identical 404 not_found envelope, including fresh commands, occupied keys, changed bodies and revoked receipt replays. Readable targets without mutation authority retain 403. Internal denial diagnostics, immutable receipts and audit history remain intact. OpenAPI and regenerated web documentation describe the deliberate unreadable 403-to-404 change; typed payloads and SQL signatures are unchanged.\n\n## Requirements and formal gate\n\nEO-003 / EO-009 / EO-045 / EO-051 / EO-055 map to CommandPrivacy.OpaqueTarget and ReadOnlyDenial, complementing ReceiptReplay and SnapshotRead. The full pinned TLC/Alloy runner passed BEFORE the SQL edit: the new paired model checked 81 generated / 49 distinct states, depth 4; both new negative configurations violated OpaqueTarget as expected. All ten negative controls were detected, the Alloy scenario was SAT and eight assertions were UNSAT within their documented scopes. This is bounded response-envelope analysis, not an unbounded or constant-time proof.\n\n## Verified local evidence\n\n- New PostgreSQL regression reproduced the old forbidden-vs-not_found leak before implementation.\n- Full scripts/verify-event-operations-formal.sh: PASS with pinned tools.\n- npm run test:event-operations-api-migration: PASS twice on fresh PostgreSQL 16, including exact JSON, RC/RR/Serializable revocation races, apply twice, rollback twice and reapply. Final checks preserve all 3 new receipts, 1 accepted transition and 9 audit entries.\n- npm run test:event-operations-http: 18 examples, 0 failures through production auth, handlers and PostgreSQL. Compares raw body/status and every non-Date header, and checks durable history and read-only denial.\n- npm run quality:repo: PASS, including 21 CI tests; heuristic audit has 0 critical/errors and 352 advisory warnings, separate from TLC/Alloy.\n- npm run test:event-operations-http-runners: 3/3 PASS. Web client regeneration, YAML parsing, shell syntax, documentation links and whitespace checks passed.\n\n## Migration, security and rollback\n\nThe API migration is still unmerged, disabled by default and outside the production manifest; only two unreadable return paths change in place. No deployed checksum, table/index or existing receipt is rewritten. Existing rollback disables/drops API entry points while preserving history; reapplication remains disabled. Do not restore the leaking behavior with the feature enabled.\n\n## Limits and manual gates\n\nIn-flight token revocation, timing/resource-exhaustion side channels, rate limiting, full mkApp/schema rehearsal, mobile/browser/offline clients and later product phases remain pending. Mobile workspace readiness failed because tdf-mobile/package.json is absent in this isolated worktree; no mobile validation is claimed. The parent still has failing hosted checks; this PR does not waive them or claim global green CI. Full evidence, exact commands and traceability are in docs/event-operations/pr-08-command-privacy.md and command-privacy-contract.md.\n\nNo merge, auto-merge, production deployment/migration, credential changes or live-money action. Production activation still requires the separate complete security and rollout review.",
